      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Set on an elevated site of approximately 0.31 hectares (0.76 acres), this attractive four-bedroom detached bungalow enjoys a wonderful setting with beautiful sea views and views of Croagh Patrick. Surrounded by a large garden and within easy reach of both Roonagh Pier and Louisburgh, the property offers an appealing combination of space, scenery and convenience, making it an ideal choice as either a family home or coastal holiday retreat.\r\nThe residence extends to c.115.5 sq.m (c.1,243 sq.ft) and has been thoughtfully extended over the years to provide bright, comfortable and versatile living accommodation.\r\nA particularly appealing feature of the home is the spacious entrance porch/sunroom. With generous glazing taking full advantage of the surrounding views, this is much more than an entrance hall. There is ample space to welcome and entertain visitors without having to bring them through the main house, while it also provides a wonderful spot to sit with a book, enjoy a morning coffee or simply relax and soak up the fantastic sea and countryside outlook.\r\nFrom here, a large internal window provides an inviting glimpse through to the heart of the home, where a warm and welcoming living room awaits. This wonderfully comfortable space features an oil range, built-in shelving and a roof light, allowing natural light to flood the room. The property also benefits from oil-fired central heating, and a newly installed top grade insulated hot water tank, ensuring warmth and comfort throughout.\r\nThe living room flows through to the generous kitchen/dining area, which, together with the adjoining living space, creates a fantastic setting for everyday family life and for entertaining friends and guests.\r\nThe traditional layout of the bungalow provides access to four bedrooms, each enjoying pleasant views towards the surrounding countryside and/or sea. A family bathroom with separate shower and an additional W.C. complete the accommodation.\r\nA rear access door provides convenient access to the garden and to the steel-tech storage shed situated adjacent to the house. The shed offers useful additional storage and has recently benefited from the installation of an electric vehicle charging point.\r\nThe spacious garden and elevated position are real highlights, providing plenty of outdoor space while allowing the property to make the most of its attractive coastal and countryside setting.\r\nThe location is particularly appealing for those wishing to enjoy the best of the West Mayo coast. Roonagh Pier is approximately 1.7km away, providing ferry access to Clare Island, while the picturesque town of Louisburgh is approximately 6km from the property.\r\nOffering four-bedroom accommodation, a large garden, an elevated setting and wonderful sea and countryside views, this is a property with broad appeal. Whether seeking a permanent family residence or a holiday home from which to enjoy this beautiful part of County Mayo, the property presents an excellent opportunity in a superb coastal location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "\tElevated site extending to c.0.76 acres with beautiful sea & views of Croagh Patrick.\r\n\tSpacious four-bedroom detached bungalow extending to c.1,243 sq.ft.\r\n\tSuperb coastal location just 1.7km from Roonagh Pier and ferry access to Clare Island\r\n\tBright, spacious entrance sunroom designed to make the most of the surrounding views.\r\n\tLarge garden offering excellent outdoor space in a peaceful countryside setting\r\n\tUseful steel tech storage shed with recently installed electric vehicle charging point. \r\n\tIdeal for use as a permanent family home or a wonderful West of Ireland holiday retreat\r\n\tWi-Fi connected making it an ideal property for those seeking to work from home"
      },
